# Assets whose byte-for-byte identity is the thing being verified.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF in the
# working tree, so the SVG's SHA-256 no longer matches the hash recorded in
# PromptHelperIcon.approved.json and the whole approved-artwork identity chain fails on
# CI while passing on the machine that generated it. These files are content, not source
# text: never translate their line endings.
*.svg           -text
*.ico           binary
*.png           binary
*.approved.json -text

# Verification inputs read by exact byte content or parsed by external tools.
*.psd1 text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
